        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): clear web push ready timeout",
        "body": "AI-assisted.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\nFixes an issue where Web Push readiness could leave behind a pending timeout even when the service worker was already ready, creating unnecessary timer buildup on repeated calls.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n`swReady()` now clears the losing timeout in a `finally` block, preserving the existing timeout rejection while cleaning up the successful path.\n\n## User Impact\nRepeated web-push checks and subscriptions stop accumulating stale readiness timers.\n\n## Evidence\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/app/web-push.runtime.test.ts`\n- `.\\node_modules\\.bin\\oxfmt.cmd --check ui\\src\\app\\web-push.runtime.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Real Chromium/Vite proof on current head `7b1f341e16bc7f480f1cdc274406ba0c2f4303af`: registered a real Service Worker, confirmed `PushManager`, called `getExistingSubscription()` 3 times, and observed `activeTimers=0` after each call and at the end.",
